============================================================================
CONSUMER RE-ENUMERATION (spec "Consumers"; split-classification defect class)
============================================================================
$ grep -rn 'ExpensesTrend|LivingExpensesTrend|HealthcareTrend|SavingsTrend|
  expenses_trend|living_expenses_trend|healthcare_trend|savings_trend'
  --include='*.go' --include='*.html' --include='*.js' (non-test, non-.swarm)
Consumers are exactly the three kpis.html sparklines (lines 53, 95, 126) plus
the struct assignment in metrics.go. No Go-side threshold is applied to a trend
array anywhere — the arrays are assigned into DashboardMetrics and read only by
the template. So there is ONE producer per figure; no split classification.
charts.js: sparkline-expenses passes no options (plain line, no clamping);
sparkline-monthly and sparkline-healthcare pass data-target only, taking
renderSparkline's hasTarget branch, whose classification is `v > target` (red)
else green — a signed negative month falls below target and fills GREEN, which
is the semantically correct reading of a refund month, and neither branch
clamps negatives out of the y series (yaxis is auto-scaled, visible:false).
data-mode="balance" (the only clamping path, `above/below` with a neutralBand)
is used ONLY by sparkline-budget over CombinedCumulativeBalance, which is CB1's
surface and is untouched. No charts.js change was needed and none was made,
consistent with the spec's "STOP and report" clause never firing.

============================================================================
OBSERVATIONS (not defects; for the lead's backlog, no criterion fails on them)
============================================================================
O1. handlers.go:1464-1469 puts currAmounts/prevAmounts into the spending-trend
    bar's `customdata` (the hover tooltip). Those are now signed, so a
    refund-dominant month's tooltip will read a negative "current" amount.
    That is consistent with the KD signed contract and with the spec's
    intent, but it is a rendered surface the spec's Consumers list did not
    name explicitly; the value is correct, so this is a note, not a finding.
O2. handlers.go:1450 colors the bar green when pctChange <= 0. With a
    refund-dominant BASE month the guard forces pctChange = 0, so the bar
    renders green ("spending decreased") for a month where no comparison was
    made. The spec explicitly accepts this as "honest degradation" and the
    committed test pins it; recording it only so the CB3 backlog has it.
O3. The four CB3-candidate sites are unchanged and confirmed verbatim above;
    handlers.go:1564-1566 in particular still subtracts |amount| for an
    outflow-typed refund (wrong direction) exactly as the lead classified.
